The sort indicator of a list column is a small chevron centred above the title.

GTK packed the sort arrow beside the column title, at its right (or left for
right-aligned titles), where it took width from the title and moved it off
the line of the unsorted columns' titles.  LikeOS lists draw a small
chevron centred at the top edge of the sorted column's header, above the
title.  The arrow is now an overlay over the title's row: centred, aligned to
the top of the header's content, 12 pixels, with the style class
"sort-indicator" so the theme can place and colour it, and passing clicks
through to the header button.  The title keeps its own alignment and no
longer moves when a column becomes sorted.

